# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mission Control — environment
#
# Nothing here is required to run the dashboard. With an empty .env the app
# boots on PGlite with seeded data and every agent runs in simulate mode.
# Fill these in as you unlock capability; see SETUP_TODO.md for what each one
# actually unblocks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset  -> local PGlite database at ./data/mission-control  (default, zero setup)
# Set    -> any Postgres (Supabase / Neon / self-hosted). Same migrations.
#           Use the Session pooler string from Supabase, not db.<ref>.supabase.co.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/postgres

# --- Agent runtime -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unset -> every agent runs in simulate mode: real activity + memory rows are
#          written and the tree updates, but no model is called.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Hard ceiling on what a single agent run may cost, in USD. Runs that would
# exceed it stop and post a blocker instead.
AGENT_MAX_COST_USD=0.50

# --- Chat channel (§6) -------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Scheduler (§7) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Unset -> /api/tick returns 503 and the cadence table never fires on its own.
#          `npm run tick` still works and is unaffected.
# Set    -> /api/tick runs whatever is due. Vercel Cron sends this as a bearer
#          token automatically; any other scheduler sends x-cron-secret.
#          Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=

# --- Integrations (§8) -------------------------------------------------------
# All optional. An agent whose source is missing reports
# "kaynak kullanilamiyor" rather than inventing a number.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# APOLLO_API_KEY=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
